LIBRARIES BUNDLED WITH THE macOS BUILD
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The macOS app ships ImageMagick's delegate libraries alongside it (they are
copied out of Homebrew by scripts/bundle-magick-mac.sh). Their licenses:

  libpng, libjpeg-turbo, libtiff, libwebp, libsharpyuv, libzstd, liblzma,
  libaom, libvmaf, little-cms2   - permissive (BSD/MIT-style)
  freetype                       - FTL or GPLv2
  libltdl (GNU Libtool)          - LGPLv2.1+
  libde265                       - LGPLv3+
  libx265                        - GPLv2+

libde265 and libx265 are pulled in only by the HEIC/AVIF coder. Building the
bundle with `scripts/bundle-magick-mac.sh --no-heic` drops that coder and leaves
no copyleft-licensed library in the app. Each library is bundled as a separate
dynamic library and is not modified beyond having its install names rewritten
for relocation; the corresponding sources are available from the upstream
projects and via Homebrew.


